Patch summary:
Backport drm_hwcomposer's fix for a lost wakeup in
DrmAtomicStateManager::ThreadFn (f84c4bf) onto the pinned Android 16 QPR2
base. The thread waited on its condition variable before checking for a new
frame or a stop request, so a notify sent while it was outside the wait was
lost: a display torn down at that moment (Ika removes one whenever an app
window closes) deadlocked in thread_.join(), and a new frame's buffers were
released late, by a synchronous cleanup on the next frame. The wait now takes
a predicate. Cuttlefish
runs drm_hwcomposer in the venus and drm_virgl GPU modes.

diff --git a/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp b/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
index 2aad05f..ec58e66 100644
--- a/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
+++ b/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
@@ -495,14 +495,13 @@ void DrmAtomicStateManager::ThreadFn() {
     {
       std::unique_lock lk(mutex_);
       base::ScopedLockAssertion lock_assertion(mutex_);
-      cv_.wait(lk);
+      cv_.wait(lk, [this, tracking_at_the_moment]() REQUIRES(mutex_) {
+        return exit_thread_ || frames_staged_ > tracking_at_the_moment;
+      });
 
       if (exit_thread_)
         break;
 
-      if (frames_staged_ <= tracking_at_the_moment)
-        continue;
-
       tracking_at_the_moment = frames_staged_;
 
       present_fence = last_present_fence_;
